Under `--additional-axioms`, a function value carries the parameter types of the lambda that built it as its domain, and two ghost functions declared with `{:functionDomain "restrict"}` and `{:functionDomain "exactDom"}` give a function's restriction to a type and whether that type is exactly its domain; every total arrow on `int`, `real`, `bool` or `ORDINAL` has an exact domain. With these, function extensionality for functions of the same exact domain can be stated as a lemma without a body; it is unsound for a domain that is not exact, such as a type parameter. The new option `--function-extensionality-axiom` adds it as an axiom triggered by an equality between two total functions of one argument (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/374).
